WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:42.836
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:43.106 --> 00:50.071
100 DAYS OF DECEPTION

3
00:50.155 --> 00:51.573
CHARACTERS, PLACES, ORGANIZATIONS, AND INCIDENTS IN THIS DRAMA ARE FICTITIOUS

4
00:51.656 --> 00:53.074
ALL CHILD ACTORS AND ANIMAL SCENES WERE FILMED UNDER GUIDELINES

5
00:59.038 --> 00:59.873
You are…

6
01:02.250 --> 01:03.501
a spy, aren't you?

7
01:10.008 --> 01:11.217
A spy from the Gugukdan.

8
01:16.014 --> 01:16.848
Yes.

9
01:18.892 --> 01:20.351
I am a spy.

10
01:21.436 --> 01:22.937
So tell them to arrest me now.

11
01:24.647 --> 01:26.733
Do I look like I'm joking?

12
01:27.525 --> 01:28.359
Yesterday,

13
01:29.194 --> 01:30.737
when the bomb went off…

14
01:30.820 --> 01:32.238
Are you okay?

15
01:33.031 --> 01:33.948
Now, let's get out.

16
01:38.786 --> 01:40.330
Why did you save me?

17
01:43.499 --> 01:44.834
I'm sorry.

18
01:48.046 --> 01:48.880
That was…

19
01:52.675 --> 01:54.344
I didn't save you.

20
01:55.887 --> 01:58.097
I just tripped.

21
02:03.436 --> 02:04.354
You're lying.

22
02:07.941 --> 02:11.027
Fine, let's say I really am a spy.

23
02:11.778 --> 02:14.906
Then do you think I'd come right out and say, "Yes, I'm a spy"?

24
02:15.782 --> 02:18.493
I don't know what made you think that.

25
02:18.576 --> 02:19.577
But I'm telling you,

26
02:20.286 --> 02:21.871
I'm really not a spy.

27
02:23.539 --> 02:26.876
Is this about yesterday's banquet bombing?

28
02:26.960 --> 02:30.255
They said some mentally disturbed Japanese man acted alone.

29
02:32.632 --> 02:33.800
But let's be honest.

30
02:34.759 --> 02:36.344
It doesn't matter if I'm a spy.

31
02:36.427 --> 02:39.597
The Government-General can call me one whenever they like.

32
02:40.640 --> 02:42.600
So what's the point of asking me?

33
02:44.227 --> 02:46.771
What is it you want me to be?

34
02:48.773 --> 02:50.817
Are you hoping I'm not a spy, or…

35
02:52.277 --> 02:53.528
that I am?

36
02:55.780 --> 02:56.990
I'm hoping you're a spy.

37
02:58.950 --> 03:01.619
Please! I'd rather you were a spy.

38
03:03.496 --> 03:04.330
At least then,

39
03:04.872 --> 03:09.002
you wouldn't be with Yoo Philip or have to endure his beatings.

40
03:09.085 --> 03:10.795
And I wouldn't have to feel…

41
03:16.050 --> 03:18.177
so confused about you anymore.

42
03:28.730 --> 03:29.564
Come in.

43
03:32.108 --> 03:33.526
Ms. Keum.

44
03:36.029 --> 03:36.988
Mr. Sato.

45
03:38.698 --> 03:40.074
Congratulations.

46
03:47.623 --> 03:48.499
Excuse me.

47
03:56.924 --> 03:58.384
Ms. Keum.

48
04:00.178 --> 04:01.262
Did you see this?

49
04:01.346 --> 04:04.265
INSPECTOR GENERAL SATO'S SON TO MARRY KIM SEUNG-EOK'S DAUGHTER

50
04:05.224 --> 04:07.477
I guess it's over for me now.

51
04:08.811 --> 04:09.687
Dad!

52
04:09.771 --> 04:10.605
EPISODE 11

53
04:14.233 --> 04:15.193
Dad.

54
04:15.276 --> 04:18.279
Good grief, Myung-nam. You're going to burst my eardrums.

55
04:18.363 --> 04:20.198
This is your doing, isn't it?

56
04:20.948 --> 04:22.325
Oh, you finally saw it.

57
04:22.825 --> 04:25.661
I wish they had printed your photo a little bigger.

58
04:25.745 --> 04:27.372
Still, that's a nice photo.

59
04:27.455 --> 04:31.376
How can I make the front page when the Government-General was bombed?

60
04:32.001 --> 04:34.045
We haven't even set a date yet.

61
04:34.128 --> 04:35.004
Oh, come on.

62
04:35.088 --> 04:37.423
I know exactly what I'm doing.

63
04:38.633 --> 04:42.261
Thanks to that headline, people will be talking about your engagement

64
04:42.345 --> 04:45.181
even more than they do about the Government-General bombing.

65
04:46.265 --> 04:48.643
They need to know that I, Kim Seung-eok,

66
04:48.726 --> 04:51.062
have the inspector general's back.

67
04:51.938 --> 04:53.106
Dad.

68
04:53.606 --> 04:56.442
Everyone makes mistakes

69
04:56.526 --> 04:58.694
and ends up losing face at some point.

70
04:59.570 --> 05:01.197
If you help at a time like that,

71
05:01.280 --> 05:03.282
you can get them on your side at little cost.

72
05:05.743 --> 05:07.662
Dad, please…

73
05:07.745 --> 05:11.290
Myung-nam, are you crying because you're moved by my wisdom?

74
05:14.585 --> 05:15.420
Yes.

75
05:16.212 --> 05:18.089
You're really something, Dad.

76
05:20.133 --> 05:22.427
Good heavens, a face like an angel, but that temper…

77
05:22.510 --> 05:24.512
What do I do about that temper of hers?

78
05:25.179 --> 05:28.558
She won't change until her husband knocks some sense into her.

79
05:30.017 --> 05:31.644
I can't even…

80
05:32.812 --> 05:34.021
It came out just fine.

81
05:44.615 --> 05:45.491
Lee Ga-kyung.

82
05:46.284 --> 05:47.452
Get a hold of yourself.

83
06:01.424 --> 06:02.717
Oh, Ms. Yamada.

84
06:04.635 --> 06:06.721
I thought you'd be at the Inspector General's Office,

85
06:06.804 --> 06:08.222
but here you are.

86
06:08.306 --> 06:10.808
I need to stop by the pneumatic tube room.

87
06:13.769 --> 06:14.770
Well then.

88
06:14.854 --> 06:15.688
I'll be off.

89
06:15.771 --> 06:16.689
Okay.

90
06:34.499 --> 06:36.501
I can't keep leaving this here.

91
06:37.668 --> 06:38.544
What should I do?

92
06:49.388 --> 06:50.223
I'm sorry.

93
06:50.306 --> 06:52.391
You've got to be kidding me!

94
06:53.059 --> 06:55.561
I paid a fortune to have this custom-made at Ginza Boutique!

95
06:55.645 --> 06:56.938
I'm so sorry.

96
06:57.021 --> 07:00.316
Who brings smelly food into the building? What were you thinking?

97
07:00.858 --> 07:01.776
I'm sorry.

98
07:01.859 --> 07:03.361
Go wipe it off in the bathroom.

99
07:04.403 --> 07:06.572
This day just keeps getting worse.

100
07:07.573 --> 07:09.408
Can you send this through the pneumatic tube?

101
07:10.576 --> 07:13.788
The inspector general asked me to send it to the governor-general's residence.

102
07:15.289 --> 07:16.624
GOVERNOR-GENERAL, IWAMURA SHIGERU

103
07:16.707 --> 07:19.335
If you hand it to Mr. Mitarai, he'll send it.

104
07:19.919 --> 07:20.795
Okay.

105
07:21.504 --> 07:22.338
Thanks.

106
07:24.173 --> 07:25.049
Sorry about that.

107
07:29.428 --> 07:32.014
Naengmyeon doesn't smell, though, right?

108
07:33.599 --> 07:34.850
I'm a Joseon person.

109
07:35.810 --> 07:36.644
I see.

110
07:36.727 --> 07:39.105
Where are you delivering that?

111
07:39.647 --> 07:40.648
It's for Mr. Toilet.

112
07:41.357 --> 07:42.191
Toilet…

113
07:44.485 --> 07:45.570
You mean Mr. Mitarai?

114
07:45.653 --> 07:46.487
Yes.

115
07:46.571 --> 07:48.030
"MITARAI," "TOILET" SAME CHARACTERS

116
07:48.114 --> 07:50.866
Normally, the customer is supposed to pick it up on the first floor.

117
07:51.492 --> 07:53.703
But "Toilet" makes me bring it inside.

118
07:53.786 --> 07:54.870
And that's every day.

119
07:54.954 --> 07:56.831
Apparently, he can't leave his post.

120
07:57.415 --> 07:59.125
He never gets tired of naengmyeon.

121
08:00.418 --> 08:01.294
Every single day?

122
08:08.092 --> 08:10.761
Operator, put me through to the governor-general's residence.

123
08:12.305 --> 08:14.765
Hello, this is the Government-General's pneumatic tube room.

124
08:14.849 --> 08:16.267
A pneumatic tube carrier is coming

125
08:16.350 --> 08:18.561
from the inspector general to the governor-general,

126
08:18.644 --> 08:19.770
so please stand by.

127
08:19.854 --> 08:20.688
Thanks.

128
08:23.232 --> 08:24.817
Hey, you, naengmyeon yobo.

129
08:24.900 --> 08:26.902
Stop dawdling and go wait outside!

130
08:33.868 --> 08:34.910
By the way,

131
08:34.994 --> 08:38.247
aren't you supposed to pick up food deliveries at the entrance?

132
08:38.331 --> 08:40.499
You think I've got all the time in the world like you?

133
08:40.583 --> 08:42.543
I don't even have time to take a bathroom break.

134
08:42.627 --> 08:44.629
It's his job to come pick up the bowls.

135
08:44.712 --> 08:46.756
Isn't that what yobos are for?

136
08:47.548 --> 08:49.175
You get lost too!

137
08:49.258 --> 08:50.217
Seriously.

138
09:01.395 --> 09:02.271
Go screw yourself.

139
09:05.858 --> 09:06.984
What did you just say?

140
09:11.781 --> 09:12.698
Use chopsticks.

141
09:12.782 --> 09:15.409
In the language of Joseon, they're called "jeotgarak."

142
09:16.160 --> 09:17.953
You just cursed at me, didn't you?

143
09:19.205 --> 09:21.290
You cursed at me in your language!

144
09:21.374 --> 09:23.709
Good heavens, of course not.

145
09:23.793 --> 09:25.127
Listen carefully.

146
09:25.211 --> 09:26.671
The English word is "chopsticks."

147
09:26.754 --> 09:28.255
In Japanese, it's "hashi."

148
09:28.339 --> 09:30.216
In the Joseon language, we say "jeotgarak."

149
09:31.008 --> 09:31.926
You little…

150
09:32.009 --> 09:34.929
Your noodles are getting soggy. You should eat them now.

151
09:35.513 --> 09:38.015
"Jeotgarak"?

152
09:43.396 --> 09:45.856
INTERPRETER TRAINEE KEUM SEO-HEE

153
09:46.816 --> 09:49.235
Since the Gugukdan was behind yesterday's attack,

154
09:50.611 --> 09:52.822
could she be one of them too?

155
09:54.532 --> 09:55.616
Gugukdan…

156
10:03.374 --> 10:04.875
I just went to the bathroom.

157
10:10.631 --> 10:13.175
It's pretty dusty. I need to do some cleaning.

158
10:13.259 --> 10:14.093
Ms. Keum.

159
10:14.176 --> 10:15.052
Right.

160
10:15.136 --> 10:17.763
I'll go check if Mr. Laurent is in yet.

161
10:17.847 --> 10:18.681
Mr. Laurent

162
10:19.348 --> 10:21.183
left Gyeongseong early this morning.

163
10:21.267 --> 10:22.101
What?

164
10:27.440 --> 10:30.276
Because he was shaken by what happened yesterday?

165
10:31.318 --> 10:32.153
Yes.

166
10:35.698 --> 10:37.366
My father and the chief of police

167
10:39.243 --> 10:41.412
are tracking down a woman from the Gugukdan.

168
10:44.457 --> 10:45.791
You should be careful too.

169
10:48.836 --> 10:49.670
My goodness.

170
10:50.254 --> 10:51.255
I told you

171
10:51.756 --> 10:53.799
I'm not a spy.

172
10:54.759 --> 10:57.386
I don't know why you're telling me this.

173
11:02.767 --> 11:04.143
Because I want to save you.

174
11:10.733 --> 11:11.567
So…

175
11:14.820 --> 11:15.654
stay safe.

176
11:22.703 --> 11:23.579
Okay.

177
11:25.247 --> 11:26.582
Thanks anyway.

178
11:27.374 --> 11:28.876
I'm not a spy, though.

179
12:37.194 --> 12:38.904
You had a high fever all night.

180
12:39.780 --> 12:42.992
I wish I could stay with you, but I have to go to work. I'm sorry.

181
12:44.159 --> 12:46.871
Call me if anything happens. I'll come right away.

182
13:26.535 --> 13:27.578
Come to think of it,

183
13:28.495 --> 13:31.206
how on earth did they get the bomb inside?

184
13:31.790 --> 13:34.960
Every entrance and passageway was under guard on the day of the banquet.

185
13:35.544 --> 13:38.088
It was impossible for outsiders to get in.

186
13:40.883 --> 13:43.052
Who'd dare bomb the Government-General?

187
13:44.637 --> 13:45.471
Exactly.

188
13:46.972 --> 13:48.766
If it was an outsider.

189
13:49.725 --> 13:50.559
Sorry?

190
13:51.185 --> 13:52.061
But then,

191
13:53.312 --> 13:56.357
doesn't a Joseon person go in and out of the Government-General every day…

192
14:03.030 --> 14:05.366
riding on an American's coattails?

193
14:22.049 --> 14:28.514
100 DAYS OF DECEPTION

194
14:39.775 --> 14:40.859
You are…

195
14:41.443 --> 14:42.611
a spy, aren't you?

196
14:44.238 --> 14:45.489
I'm hoping you're a spy.

197
14:45.990 --> 14:47.908
And I wouldn't have to feel…

198
14:49.910 --> 14:51.829
so confused about you anymore.

199
14:54.623 --> 14:55.916
I saw it myself.

200
14:57.167 --> 14:58.335
Sato Hideo

201
14:59.253 --> 15:01.130
murdered Songjeon.

202
15:02.089 --> 15:03.465
Because I want to save you.

203
15:04.800 --> 15:07.678
So… stay safe.

204
15:14.435 --> 15:16.562
None of this adds up.

205
15:29.992 --> 15:30.826
What the…

206
15:31.368 --> 15:33.662
Who do you think you're trying to steal from?

207
15:33.746 --> 15:34.580
What the hell?

208
15:35.497 --> 15:37.666
You picked the wrong person to mess with. I've been…

209
15:40.794 --> 15:41.628
Wait.

210
15:42.755 --> 15:43.589
Lee No-ma.

211
15:44.173 --> 15:45.716
Lee Ga-kyung?

212
15:52.097 --> 15:53.682
What? The Government-General?

213
15:56.935 --> 16:00.022
You're telling me you work for the Government-General?

214
16:00.773 --> 16:01.607
Yes.

215
16:04.902 --> 16:09.364
Come on, Ga-kyung, you're just teasing me because it's been so long.

216
16:09.448 --> 16:11.158
Come on, let me see your fingers.

217
16:11.241 --> 16:12.076
You're…

218
16:12.826 --> 16:13.786
not crossing them.

219
16:13.869 --> 16:15.329
Seriously? Did you really…

220
16:16.830 --> 16:18.290
get a job at the Government-General?

221
16:20.584 --> 16:21.418
Yeah.

222
16:27.007 --> 16:27.925
Unbelievable.

223
16:30.135 --> 16:31.220
I know you love money

224
16:31.303 --> 16:33.806
and couldn't care less about Joseon's independence,

225
16:33.889 --> 16:35.849
but how could you work for the Government-General?

226
16:37.351 --> 16:40.354
I heard the Gugukdan bombed the Government-General yesterday.

227
16:40.437 --> 16:41.355
Bam!

228
16:42.189 --> 16:43.607
Those Japanese police went…

229
16:43.690 --> 16:46.026
Bak-chun heard about it and told us.

230
16:46.110 --> 16:48.487
The whole neighborhood was so thrilled.

231
16:48.570 --> 16:50.948
You're holding it upside down.

232
16:51.031 --> 16:52.324
How did you know?

233
16:53.450 --> 16:56.036
Some people would die for Joseon's independence.

234
16:56.662 --> 16:58.539
Ga-kyung, you're a Joseon person too.

235
16:58.622 --> 17:01.291
And hey, we're friends.

236
17:01.375 --> 17:04.002
Think about how my parents died during the Manse Movement,

237
17:04.086 --> 17:05.546
and about Kkot-nim.

238
17:05.629 --> 17:08.257
So how can you possibly work for them?

239
17:08.340 --> 17:09.925
No, you can't.

240
17:15.848 --> 17:18.016
I'm sorry, No-ma.

241
17:23.230 --> 17:24.189
Yeah.

242
17:25.190 --> 17:27.151
Okay. Sure.

243
17:28.777 --> 17:29.611
I get it.

244
17:30.279 --> 17:31.321
So, yeah…

245
17:33.407 --> 17:34.700
Remember your ointment.

246
17:34.783 --> 17:36.243
No-ma, wait.

247
17:44.918 --> 17:47.546
Kkot-nim was really sick.

248
17:47.629 --> 17:50.841
She was really sick?

249
17:52.009 --> 17:54.011
Why? What's wrong? How is she now?

250
17:54.094 --> 17:56.221
She's a little better now.

251
17:56.847 --> 17:58.932
But even when she was burning up and moaning in pain,

252
18:00.392 --> 18:01.518
she kept asking for you.

253
18:02.561 --> 18:05.147
I get you couldn't talk about working for the Government-General,

254
18:05.230 --> 18:07.065
but how could you not come see Kkot-nim?

255
18:08.984 --> 18:11.987
Were you trying to cut us out of your life completely?

256
18:30.547 --> 18:31.924
There's nothing suspicious.

257
18:35.886 --> 18:38.639
There are two Josenjings working here.

258
18:38.722 --> 18:41.475
But there's nothing suspicious here?

259
18:41.558 --> 18:42.601
Chief.

260
18:48.649 --> 18:50.609
SIN TAE-JIN

261
18:51.360 --> 18:53.070
A pawn ticket?

262
18:53.654 --> 18:54.529
What?

263
18:55.155 --> 18:56.323
What did you just say?

264
18:59.826 --> 19:02.412
That I think Sato Hideo

265
19:03.914 --> 19:05.916
has started to suspect I'm a spy.

266
19:05.999 --> 19:07.376
But how…

267
19:14.591 --> 19:17.094
Why? How could you let him find out?

268
19:18.220 --> 19:19.054
Well…

269
19:21.139 --> 19:22.349
I'm not sure.

270
19:24.685 --> 19:26.728
I told him I wasn't a spy, but…

271
19:31.858 --> 19:33.944
Don't trail off and finish your sentence.

272
19:34.528 --> 19:36.655
What exactly did Sato Hideo say?

273
19:36.738 --> 19:39.825
How on earth did he catch on?

274
19:40.867 --> 19:41.868
That must be why

275
19:43.161 --> 19:45.872
Sato Hideo came here last night.

276
19:45.956 --> 19:47.541
He was looking for solid proof.

277
19:49.835 --> 19:52.879
So, you told him it wasn't true.

278
19:52.963 --> 19:53.922
What else did you say?

279
19:54.756 --> 19:56.633
I told him he was seriously mistaken

280
19:57.175 --> 19:58.760
and that it wasn't true at all.

281
20:00.721 --> 20:01.555
But…

282
20:02.931 --> 20:03.807
But?

283
20:08.270 --> 20:10.897
He said the inspector general and the chief of police

284
20:10.981 --> 20:13.525
were after some woman from the Gugukdan.

285
20:15.944 --> 20:17.321
He warned me to be careful.

286
20:17.404 --> 20:18.697
That's what Sato Hideo said.

287
20:22.534 --> 20:24.244
Why would he tell you that?

288
20:25.871 --> 20:27.456
I'm not sure why he did.

289
20:28.040 --> 20:30.125
He's trying to win your trust so he can catch us.

290
20:30.208 --> 20:31.043
Don't fall for it.

291
20:33.503 --> 20:34.379
Okay.

292
20:37.966 --> 20:39.343
Because I want to save you.

293
20:41.636 --> 20:43.764
You have to get a hold of yourself.

294
20:43.847 --> 20:45.182
You can't fall for it.

295
20:45.682 --> 20:46.516
Do you hear me?

296
20:48.769 --> 20:49.603
Yes.

297
20:51.271 --> 20:53.273
We need to tell our comrades right away.

298
21:11.333 --> 21:12.334
Mr. Hideo.

299
21:14.336 --> 21:15.462
Good evening.

300
21:17.214 --> 21:18.924
What brings you here at this hour?

301
21:19.758 --> 21:21.468
I'm sorry to drop by so late.

302
21:21.551 --> 21:23.637
The police visit yesterday must've been unpleasant.

303
21:23.720 --> 21:27.349
I wanted to apologize and thank you for the article you wrote today.

304
21:27.432 --> 21:28.558
So I thought I'd drop by.

305
21:30.018 --> 21:32.104
You didn't have to come all the way here.

306
21:32.187 --> 21:33.355
In any case, thank you.

307
21:35.857 --> 21:36.691
All right then.

308
21:37.609 --> 21:38.527
How about a drink?

309
21:40.529 --> 21:42.447
Tomorrow happens to be a holiday.

310
21:58.338 --> 22:01.216
Yanagi. You know how to write Joseon characters, right?

311
22:01.299 --> 22:03.176
Write the word "big brother" for me.

312
22:16.022 --> 22:17.065
BIG BROTHER

313
22:21.987 --> 22:24.406
FATHER

314
22:26.199 --> 22:28.368
Does this mean "big brother" in the Joseon language?

315
22:29.619 --> 22:31.413
This says "oppa."

316
22:31.496 --> 22:33.665
It means "big brother."

317
22:33.748 --> 22:35.500
This means "father."

318
22:36.084 --> 22:37.377
Abeoji.

319
22:38.211 --> 22:39.921
"Oppa."

320
22:40.005 --> 22:41.548
"Abeoji."

321
22:44.759 --> 22:47.053
Then, what about "mother"?

322
22:59.191 --> 23:00.901
"Eomeoni."

323
23:01.568 --> 23:03.528
So that's what it looks like.

324
23:03.612 --> 23:05.238
"Mother" in the Joseon letters.

325
23:06.031 --> 23:06.865
Yanagi.

326
23:06.948 --> 23:09.951
What did my mother look like?

327
23:11.203 --> 23:14.331
Not the one from the Sato family who passed away last year.

328
23:14.414 --> 23:17.667
I mean the Joseon mother who gave birth to me.

329
23:18.877 --> 23:22.130
I don't even have a single picture of her.

330
23:25.550 --> 23:28.845
Mrs. Sato would always glare at me.

331
23:29.721 --> 23:32.724
She'd beat me when Father wasn't around.

332
23:33.391 --> 23:34.935
It hurt so much.

333
23:35.435 --> 23:37.854
She never said anything to Hideo,

334
23:38.438 --> 23:40.774
but when he and Father weren't around,

335
23:41.858 --> 23:45.946
she'd call me a filthy Josenjing.

336
23:47.364 --> 23:50.992
She was so nasty. No wonder she was sick right up until she died.

337
23:54.955 --> 23:55.872
Yanagi.

338
23:56.623 --> 23:59.209
What was my mother like?

339
23:59.292 --> 24:01.169
You remember her, don't you?

340
24:01.253 --> 24:02.337
Was she pretty?

341
24:02.420 --> 24:04.089
What were her eyes like?

342
24:04.172 --> 24:05.173
What about her nose?

343
24:05.257 --> 24:06.258
And her lips?

344
24:07.342 --> 24:11.763
She was so much prettier than Mrs. Sato, wasn't she?

345
24:36.371 --> 24:37.247
Yanagi.

346
24:38.623 --> 24:41.626
She died giving birth to me.

347
24:44.713 --> 24:47.757
That's why Father hates me, right?

348
24:57.684 --> 24:59.019
You're home, sir.

349
24:59.978 --> 25:01.229
I'm sorry.

350
25:02.480 --> 25:05.358
I didn't realize you had come home.

351
25:06.067 --> 25:07.277
Welcome home.

352
25:14.784 --> 25:15.910
I'll clean it up now.

353
25:51.696 --> 25:53.782
You can't even look me in the eye.

354
25:55.867 --> 25:56.785
Are you

355
25:57.869 --> 25:58.703
scared of me?

356
25:59.579 --> 26:01.373
I'm sorry, Father.

357
26:03.875 --> 26:05.293
Your mother…

358
26:13.343 --> 26:15.637
didn't fear me in the slightest.

359
26:18.682 --> 26:19.849
I'm sorry.

360
26:19.933 --> 26:22.310
I won't do it again, Father.

361
26:24.854 --> 26:25.730
Yanagi.

362
26:27.107 --> 26:29.275
I'm sorry, sir.

363
26:29.359 --> 26:31.277
I shouldn't have done that.

364
26:32.112 --> 26:32.987
Use this

365
26:34.447 --> 26:35.573
to start the fire.

366
26:36.741 --> 26:39.202
Yes, as you wish.

367
26:47.585 --> 26:48.420
Where's Hideo?

368
26:48.503 --> 26:51.464
He hasn't come home yet.

369
27:22.454 --> 27:24.205
Seo-hee brought some chocolate.

370
27:25.665 --> 27:28.126
Hope you have a good time.

371
27:29.252 --> 27:30.086
Are you leaving?

372
27:32.464 --> 27:34.716
Come have a seat. You already know each other.

373
27:39.763 --> 27:40.638
Sure.

374
27:55.779 --> 27:57.739
My wife is taking a bath at the moment.

375
27:58.323 --> 28:00.950
Seo-hee and I were about to enjoy some time together.

376
28:01.034 --> 28:02.285
You've ruined the moment.

377
28:05.580 --> 28:06.414
Oh dear.

378
28:07.749 --> 28:09.459
Looks like I'm an unwelcome guest.

379
28:11.836 --> 28:13.254
But since I'm already here,

380
28:13.838 --> 28:15.465
you may as well keep up the act.

381
28:26.142 --> 28:29.521
I heard you asked Seo-hee today if she was a spy.

382
28:30.772 --> 28:31.606
Yes.

383
28:34.526 --> 28:37.570
She may have sticky fingers, but she's hardly a spy.

384
28:39.113 --> 28:41.074
She's just a hopeless romantic.

385
28:45.995 --> 28:47.247
A romantic, you say…

386
28:49.457 --> 28:52.252
You mean people who'd risk their lives for love?

387
28:53.169 --> 28:54.003
Exactly.

388
29:00.218 --> 29:03.388
Some people would put their lives on the line for other things.

389
29:04.681 --> 29:05.598
For example…

390
29:08.476 --> 29:10.937
the independence of Joseon or something like that.

391
29:17.026 --> 29:18.486
The independence of Joseon?

392
29:20.280 --> 29:22.240
Just as some people would die for love,

393
29:23.283 --> 29:26.035
others would risk their lives for Joseon's independence.

394
29:29.581 --> 29:31.207
What do you think drives them?

395
29:32.917 --> 29:34.377
What could possibly make them

396
29:34.961 --> 29:36.588
go that far?

397
29:37.589 --> 29:39.674
They might never even live to see independence.

398
29:39.757 --> 29:41.009
And even if it comes,

399
29:41.885 --> 29:44.137
what's the point if they're already dead?

400
29:50.143 --> 29:54.480
Of everyone I've met, no one believes in love as deeply as you do.

401
29:55.440 --> 29:57.066
I just started wondering

402
29:57.692 --> 29:59.319
how you feel about those people.

403
30:04.782 --> 30:05.617
I'm not sure.

404
30:07.368 --> 30:10.330
I'm an American, born and raised in Hawaii,

405
30:10.413 --> 30:13.166
so I can't fully understand how they feel.

406
30:15.835 --> 30:18.463
But the Joseon laborers in Hawaii's sugar plantations

407
30:18.546 --> 30:21.090
teach their children to speak the Joseon language,

408
30:21.174 --> 30:24.385
knowing their kids might never even visit their homeland.

409
30:26.262 --> 30:30.391
And they scrape together every penny to send money to the independence cause.

410
30:30.475 --> 30:33.061
All while they can't afford to put butter on their kids' bread.

411
30:34.938 --> 30:36.522
They're a rather foolish bunch.

412
30:39.359 --> 30:41.778
Every time I asked, they all said the same thing.

413
30:42.570 --> 30:44.489
"Because I love my country."

414
30:44.572 --> 30:45.490
That was all.

415
30:47.825 --> 30:49.243
Wouldn't it be scary?

416
30:50.995 --> 30:51.829
To love…

417
30:54.707 --> 30:56.167
To love something that much.

418
31:03.132 --> 31:05.677
One Joseon man in Hawaii once told me this.

419
31:05.760 --> 31:08.054
There's nothing frightening about loving someone.

420
31:14.102 --> 31:18.189
What's truly frightening is losing them and having to keep living.

421
31:27.448 --> 31:29.492
I hope you find a love like that

422
31:29.993 --> 31:32.704
for yourself someday, Mr. Hideo.

423
31:32.787 --> 31:35.915
I meant no offense, especially with your wedding coming up.

424
31:35.999 --> 31:37.792
I saw the article about your engagement.

425
31:37.875 --> 31:39.585
It was all over the front page.

426
31:42.296 --> 31:43.172
I also saw…

427
31:44.549 --> 31:47.010
the article you wrote about the banquet yesterday.

428
31:49.012 --> 31:51.472
I came to thank you for that, but I nearly forgot.

429
31:52.140 --> 31:52.974
Thank you.

430
31:54.851 --> 31:55.768
Much obliged.

431
32:02.567 --> 32:03.443
Well then,

432
32:04.736 --> 32:05.862
I'd better get going.

433
32:24.964 --> 32:26.883
Do you believe people can change?

434
32:28.593 --> 32:29.677
Even for…

435
32:32.638 --> 32:36.184
someone like me who's never felt anything like that?

436
32:38.311 --> 32:39.187
Absolutely.

437
32:41.314 --> 32:43.733
Don't we all dream of that kind of love?

438
32:46.903 --> 32:47.904
Ms. Keum…

439
32:49.530 --> 32:50.782
do you think so too?

440
33:02.251 --> 33:03.127
Yes.

441
33:05.004 --> 33:08.549
I think people can change.

442
33:16.390 --> 33:17.517
Well, Mr. Hideo.

443
33:18.392 --> 33:20.186
You're the inspector general's son,

444
33:20.269 --> 33:22.313
yet you want to understand those people.

445
33:23.272 --> 33:25.233
That's incredibly admirable.

446
33:26.526 --> 33:30.196
Even so, in their eyes, you're nothing more than Japan's lapdog.

447
33:38.246 --> 33:40.373
I apologize if I've offended you.

448
33:40.456 --> 33:42.416
Perhaps I've had one too many.

449
33:58.266 --> 33:59.100
What?

450
33:59.684 --> 34:01.352
There's no Jongno Pawnshop in Jongno?

451
34:01.435 --> 34:02.270
No, sir.

452
34:02.353 --> 34:03.855
There were similar names

453
34:03.938 --> 34:06.858
like "The First Jongno Pawnshop" or "Jungno Pawnshop."

454
34:06.941 --> 34:09.652
There were over 20 pawnshops with similar names.

455
34:09.735 --> 34:12.155
But none of them was called "Jongno Pawnshop."

456
34:12.238 --> 34:15.658
Not only does it not exist today, but it didn't exist in 1919 either,

457
34:15.741 --> 34:17.743
the year indicated on the pawn ticket.

458
34:17.827 --> 34:19.203
What about Sin Tae-jin?

459
34:21.539 --> 34:24.167
Don't tell me you couldn't find that name either.

460
34:24.250 --> 34:25.084
That's right.

461
34:25.585 --> 34:27.795
The name Sin Tae-jin didn't appear on the wanted list

462
34:27.879 --> 34:30.173
for independence fighters or in any prison records.

463
34:30.256 --> 34:33.301
And we couldn't find anyone who knew Interpreter Sato

464
34:33.384 --> 34:34.343
by his Joseon name.

465
34:38.848 --> 34:40.308
Jongno Pawnshop…

466
34:40.975 --> 34:42.226
Sin Tae-jin…

467
34:54.405 --> 34:55.781
What did you just say?

468
34:55.865 --> 34:57.700
Her cover's been blown?

469
34:59.035 --> 35:01.996
Yes, apparently, Sato Hideo confronted her directly.

470
35:02.079 --> 35:03.247
Though she denied it.

471
35:03.873 --> 35:05.625
Sato Hideo…

472
35:06.209 --> 35:09.503
As if killing Songjeon weren't enough, now he's up to something.

473
35:10.213 --> 35:12.173
First, we need to get her out of there.

474
35:12.256 --> 35:14.634
We can't let her stay at the Government-General.

475
35:14.717 --> 35:16.469
But if she quits,

476
35:17.178 --> 35:19.055
won't they take it as proof that she's a spy?

477
35:19.138 --> 35:22.350
Even so, we can't just do nothing when her cover's already blown.

478
35:22.433 --> 35:25.770
There's also a chance Sato Hideo's turned her against us.

479
35:25.853 --> 35:29.148
We got her to spy for us with money and a chance to go to America.

480
35:29.232 --> 35:30.733
She might have accepted a better deal

481
35:30.816 --> 35:33.069
and started setting a trap for us.

482
35:33.152 --> 35:34.278
That's enough.

483
35:34.362 --> 35:36.113
We can't make baseless assumptions.

484
35:38.658 --> 35:40.618
We'll say our affair is over,

485
35:40.701 --> 35:42.286
fire her, and send her to Shanghai.

486
35:43.454 --> 35:44.288
Shanghai?

487
35:45.331 --> 35:48.125
She's been dreaming of going to America. Won't that cause trouble?

488
35:48.209 --> 35:51.545
Then wouldn't it be better to get rid of her?

489
35:52.129 --> 35:53.214
Chi-gun!

490
35:53.297 --> 35:56.008
Should she get caught on the way to Shanghai and talk,

491
35:56.092 --> 35:57.635
it'll be the end of all of us.

492
35:57.718 --> 36:00.888
However strong someone's will is, torture can break anyone.

493
36:00.972 --> 36:01.847
Even so…

494
36:01.931 --> 36:03.266
Yes, I know.

495
36:03.349 --> 36:07.061
Cheol-yong endured Sato's torture at Jongno Police Station

496
36:07.979 --> 36:09.689
and ten years in Seodaemun Prison.

497
36:11.232 --> 36:13.985
The difference is, he believed in Joseon's independence.

498
36:15.444 --> 36:17.405
That girl has no such belief, does she?

499
36:20.074 --> 36:20.908
Fine.

500
36:23.661 --> 36:26.747
So in the end, a spy is doomed to die.

501
36:26.831 --> 36:29.166
They either get caught and killed or we kill them.

502
36:34.338 --> 36:35.715
Since when have we treated

503
36:35.798 --> 36:38.175
the lives of innocent Joseon people so lightly?

504
36:39.010 --> 36:41.679
And remember, she trusted us and worked for our cause.

505
36:42.305 --> 36:44.432
She gave up her dream of going to America,

506
36:44.515 --> 36:46.600
and came back to save our lives.

507
36:46.684 --> 36:50.271
But all our lives are on the line.

508
36:50.354 --> 36:54.150
Then let's ask someone who's served our cause as a spy for a long time.

509
36:54.233 --> 36:55.109
Suzuki.

510
36:56.777 --> 36:58.029
I mean, Seog-won.

511
37:02.408 --> 37:05.411
Thirteen years ago, when I was studying in Tokyo,

512
37:05.494 --> 37:09.457
I accepted Un-hak's offer to become a spy and joined the Gugukdan.

513
37:10.624 --> 37:12.543
I was willing to risk my life then,

514
37:13.878 --> 37:14.962
and I still am.

515
37:17.506 --> 37:18.382
But…

516
37:20.051 --> 37:21.177
she's still young.

517
37:21.927 --> 37:24.430
I want to make sure she gets out of this safely.

518
37:28.976 --> 37:30.936
Yes, understood.

519
37:31.771 --> 37:34.231
And I'm sorry for what I said. I meant…

520
37:34.315 --> 37:36.567
I understand. It's all right.

521
37:39.278 --> 37:41.530
I'll come up with the money to keep her quiet.

522
37:42.198 --> 37:43.908
We owe you yet another favor.

523
37:43.991 --> 37:45.659
You're all risking your lives.

524
37:46.577 --> 37:48.621
Selling a few pieces of gold is nothing.

525
37:50.289 --> 37:51.499
We should all lie low

526
37:52.124 --> 37:53.459
for the time being.

527
37:53.542 --> 37:55.628
We can't keep hiding forever.

528
37:57.421 --> 37:59.465
We need to get rid of Sato Hideo.

529
38:07.181 --> 38:08.724
Kkot-nim.

530
38:08.808 --> 38:12.061
Ga-kyung, I missed you so much.

531
38:12.895 --> 38:14.897
Have you been well, Kkot-nim?

532
38:15.773 --> 38:17.358
Oh dear, I heard you were sick.

533
38:18.067 --> 38:19.402
You're skin and bones now.

534
38:19.902 --> 38:21.237
I'm okay.

535
38:21.320 --> 38:22.655
Are you back from America?

536
38:22.738 --> 38:24.615
Are you going to live with us again?

537
38:25.616 --> 38:26.742
No.

538
38:26.826 --> 38:28.994
I have to go back to America.

539
38:30.454 --> 38:33.749
Look what I got for you, Kkot-nim.

540
38:35.584 --> 38:37.586
Ta-da! Chocolate.

541
38:37.670 --> 38:39.296
Wow, chocolate!

542
38:39.380 --> 38:41.048
Did you get this in America?

543
38:41.132 --> 38:44.051
I sure did. I bought it in America.

544
38:45.344 --> 38:49.765
America? More like with your Government-General paycheck.

545
38:49.849 --> 38:51.517
What? What general?

546
38:52.101 --> 38:53.144
-Kkot-nim. -Never mind.

547
38:53.227 --> 38:54.228
Chocolate.

548
38:56.605 --> 38:57.565
How is it?

549
38:58.065 --> 38:59.358
It's so yummy!

550
38:59.442 --> 39:00.276
Do you like it?

551
39:02.445 --> 39:05.156
When will you come back from America next time?

552
39:06.365 --> 39:10.411
Can't you come whenever the boss goes to church for rice cakes, like today?

553
39:11.036 --> 39:14.498
My teacher comes on the days the boss goes to church too.

554
39:14.582 --> 39:15.541
What?

555
39:16.292 --> 39:17.126
There he is!

556
39:17.793 --> 39:19.336
Teacher!

557
39:20.463 --> 39:24.467
Hey, why didn't you tell me Kkot-nim had her reading lesson today?

558
39:24.550 --> 39:25.801
What did you say?

559
39:26.886 --> 39:28.304
How are you doing, Kkot-nim?

560
39:33.684 --> 39:36.520
Wait, do you two know each other?

561
39:37.646 --> 39:38.898
Teacher.

562
39:39.732 --> 39:41.233
This is great!

563
39:41.317 --> 39:45.446
Ga-kyung is here, and so is my hangul teacher!

564
39:45.529 --> 39:47.239
Hello.

565
39:47.865 --> 39:48.699
"Ga-kyung"?

566
39:50.284 --> 39:52.411
So you have hangul lessons today.

567
39:52.495 --> 39:54.580
If I'd known, I wouldn't have come today.

568
39:54.663 --> 39:56.207
I should get going.

569
39:57.416 --> 39:58.375
Kkot-nim.

570
40:00.753 --> 40:01.712
Ga-kyung?

571
40:02.505 --> 40:03.631
Is that you, Ga-kyung?

572
40:06.342 --> 40:07.551
It is you, Lee Ga-kyung!

573
40:08.260 --> 40:09.512
Didn't you go to America?

574
40:10.930 --> 40:12.598
Geum-ok, that's--

575
40:12.681 --> 40:13.891
You rotten thing!

576
40:14.475 --> 40:15.684
Why are you hitting me?

577
40:15.768 --> 40:18.395
How could you vanish without a word, you rotten thing?

578
40:18.479 --> 40:19.480
You deserve a beating.

579
40:20.022 --> 40:20.856
That hurts!

580
40:21.398 --> 40:22.608
Your rubber shoes!

581
40:22.691 --> 40:23.984
Do they fit okay?

582
40:24.068 --> 40:26.153
Yeah, they fit perfectly.

583
40:26.237 --> 40:29.615
Thanks to these, my toes stay off the dirty ground.

584
40:29.698 --> 40:31.158
I'm glad. I'd better go now.

585
40:31.909 --> 40:32.910
Stop distracting me.

586
40:32.993 --> 40:34.578
-I'm going to whack you with this. -No.

587
40:34.662 --> 40:36.288
Wait, stop, that hurts!

588
40:36.372 --> 40:38.499
-Get over here. -You'll mess up your shoes!

589
40:38.582 --> 40:39.416
Hello.

590
40:40.501 --> 40:41.335
Hello.

591
40:42.836 --> 40:43.754
Kkot-nim.

592
40:44.338 --> 40:45.381
What was her name again?

593
40:45.464 --> 40:49.343
Her name is Lee Ga-kyung. Lee Ga-kyung.

594
40:57.434 --> 40:58.435
Nice to meet you…

595
41:03.899 --> 41:04.775
Ms. Lee Ga-kyung.

596
41:23.419 --> 41:24.253
Oh, right.

597
41:24.795 --> 41:26.672
I've got another letter from my brother.

598
41:31.218 --> 41:32.803
IM GEUM-OK

599
41:38.517 --> 41:39.893
Dear Geum-ok,

600
41:40.686 --> 41:43.856
my name is Kim Seok-gu. I've been staying with Geum-deok.

601
41:44.815 --> 41:47.359
Geum-deok talked about you a lot.

602
41:47.443 --> 41:48.569
What is it?

603
41:49.486 --> 41:51.488
Is he asking me to send him money again?

604
41:57.661 --> 42:00.914
Geum-deok worked hard, but he got sick from hunger.

605
42:01.749 --> 42:03.959
The farm wouldn't pay him.

606
42:05.336 --> 42:08.464
He asked them many times to pay him, but they beat him instead.

607
42:09.256 --> 42:10.966
He said he wanted to go home.

608
42:12.176 --> 42:14.595
Those were his final words.

609
42:16.263 --> 42:17.222
I'm sorry.

610
42:19.725 --> 42:20.809
Is that what it says?

611
42:21.935 --> 42:23.228
That little punk.

612
42:23.312 --> 42:26.273
He knows I'm barely putting food on the table by weaving straw mats.

613
42:26.357 --> 42:28.400
And if he dares ask me for money again…

614
42:29.902 --> 42:30.819
It says Geum-deok…

615
42:33.614 --> 42:35.240
gets white rice with every meal.

616
42:35.991 --> 42:37.910
White rice?

617
42:37.993 --> 42:38.827
For real?

618
42:39.328 --> 42:41.955
He left for Manchuria because we couldn't even afford barley rice.

619
42:43.123 --> 42:45.584
He's eating well and doing fine.

620
42:46.835 --> 42:49.630
He says Manchurian winters are brutal, but it's been warmer lately.

621
42:53.967 --> 42:56.428
And he says he used the money you sent

622
42:58.138 --> 42:59.515
to buy himself new clothes.

623
43:02.893 --> 43:04.228
And this is all I've got.

624
43:04.728 --> 43:06.063
He's living the good life.

625
43:07.981 --> 43:08.816
That's not all.

626
43:08.899 --> 43:11.443
Guess why Geum-deok bought new clothes?

627
43:11.527 --> 43:12.945
-Why? -Look here.

628
43:13.028 --> 43:14.905
He found a girl he likes.

629
43:14.988 --> 43:15.823
What?

630
43:16.407 --> 43:17.700
Hey, in that case…

631
43:17.783 --> 43:18.659
Oh my goodness.

632
43:18.742 --> 43:20.869
No wonder he needed money.

633
43:22.121 --> 43:24.206
He's a sharp kid, that one.

634
43:26.834 --> 43:29.753
Geum-deok says he's going to be pretty busy from now on.

635
43:30.587 --> 43:32.631
So even if you don't hear from him much,

636
43:33.841 --> 43:34.925
don't be concerned.

637
43:35.008 --> 43:37.094
Who cares about letters now?

638
43:37.177 --> 43:39.555
My little brother is about to get married.

639
43:41.223 --> 43:42.599
-That's great. -Geum-ok.

640
43:42.683 --> 43:44.518
That's wonderful news.

641
43:44.601 --> 43:45.602
Tell me about it.

642
43:45.686 --> 43:47.396
Should I send him some more money?

643
44:02.661 --> 44:03.871
Are you serious?

644
44:07.666 --> 44:09.918
You won't listen unless I do this, will you?

645
44:10.669 --> 44:12.921
Oh dear.

646
44:13.005 --> 44:14.673
How could we leave our homes?

647
44:14.757 --> 44:18.343
What a load of rot!

648
44:18.886 --> 44:20.554
That's right! And listen.

649
44:20.637 --> 44:23.265
This is my home. Where am I supposed to go?

650
44:23.348 --> 44:25.976
We've sent you plenty of demolition notices already.

651
44:26.059 --> 44:26.894
Here, look.

652
44:26.977 --> 44:28.437
Demolition notices?

653
44:28.520 --> 44:30.522
We know nothing about that. What do you mean?

654
44:30.606 --> 44:32.649
You wouldn't know because you can't read.

655
44:32.733 --> 44:34.610
Are you telling us to become homeless?

656
44:34.693 --> 44:37.112
That's your problem to figure out, damn it!

657
44:37.196 --> 44:39.865
You wouldn't dare say a word to the Japs!

658
44:39.948 --> 44:42.409
Why do you come here

659
44:42.493 --> 44:44.912
and bully your own people? Just why?

660
44:44.995 --> 44:47.748
You live in a shack next to graves. What are you complaining about?

661
44:47.831 --> 44:48.999
What's wrong with the graves?

662
44:49.583 --> 44:50.793
This is our home!

663
44:51.376 --> 44:54.546
Where in Joseon isn't there a grave?

664
44:54.630 --> 44:58.467
People have lived and died on this land for 5,000 years.

665
44:59.051 --> 45:00.219
So what?

666
45:00.302 --> 45:02.054
You call this shack a home?

667
45:02.137 --> 45:03.680
Even dogs wouldn't live here.

668
45:04.890 --> 45:06.225
What? Did you just hit me?

669
45:06.809 --> 45:08.685
You say even dogs wouldn't live here?

670
45:09.645 --> 45:12.356
The dogs are all living there

671
45:13.065 --> 45:15.400
at the Government-General.

672
45:15.484 --> 45:17.486
Those sons of bitches.

673
45:18.403 --> 45:20.531
Damn Japs, those sons of bitches!

674
45:21.406 --> 45:24.618
You're nothing but their stooges!

675
45:26.829 --> 45:28.705
Ruff, ruff! Bark like a dog.

676
45:29.581 --> 45:30.999
Ruff, ruff!

677
45:31.083 --> 45:32.251
-Ruff! -What the hell?

678
45:32.334 --> 45:33.544
-What's with her? -Go on, bark.

679
45:33.627 --> 45:35.003
-Hey, grab her! -Ruff, ruff!

680
45:35.087 --> 45:36.505
You crazy bitch!

681
45:37.714 --> 45:38.966
You scoundrels!

682
45:39.049 --> 45:40.759
My baby! My baby.

683
45:42.135 --> 45:42.970
No.

684
45:44.221 --> 45:45.931
She's seriously insane.

685
45:46.014 --> 45:47.558
You bastard!

686
45:47.641 --> 45:48.976
Should I trample you too?

687
45:49.059 --> 45:49.935
Should I trample you?

688
45:54.857 --> 45:56.859
Oh no.

689
45:59.486 --> 46:00.696
You bastard!

690
46:01.655 --> 46:03.448
You hurt my baby!

691
46:03.532 --> 46:05.200
-Stop her! -You!

692
46:07.452 --> 46:08.829
She's gone mad!

693
46:11.915 --> 46:15.252
She's unwell. She's not well!

694
46:15.335 --> 46:16.628
Oh yeah?

695
46:16.712 --> 46:18.255
I'll make you feel a whole lot worse.

696
46:18.338 --> 46:19.965
You wait right there.

697
46:20.048 --> 46:22.009
-Get over here! -Cut it out!

698
46:22.092 --> 46:24.720
Who are you telling me to stop, you crippled bastard!

699
46:26.972 --> 46:27.848
Mr. Lee!

700
46:28.640 --> 46:30.267
You bunch of filthy lowlifes.

701
46:31.268 --> 46:32.519
You all got a death wish?

702
46:32.603 --> 46:33.562
Are you okay?

703
46:34.396 --> 46:35.230
Your leg…

704
46:35.898 --> 46:37.816
How could you beat people up?

705
46:37.900 --> 46:40.736
You're no better than animals, you filthy lowlifes!

706
46:41.320 --> 46:42.195
Geum-ok!

707
46:43.822 --> 46:44.990
Who are you people?

708
46:45.073 --> 46:47.159
What gives you the right to barge into--

709
46:47.242 --> 46:48.702
And who the hell are you?

710
46:48.785 --> 46:49.870
I said, who are you?

711
46:51.121 --> 46:51.955
Don't touch her.

712
46:53.290 --> 46:54.249
Look at this punk.

713
46:55.334 --> 46:56.251
Let go.

714
46:56.335 --> 46:57.210
I said let go!

715
46:57.294 --> 46:58.712
Hands off! You hear me?

716
47:01.423 --> 47:02.257
Let go!

717
47:02.925 --> 47:04.176
What? Are you sure?

718
47:07.846 --> 47:09.640
I'm going to kill you today.

719
47:17.230 --> 47:18.732
-You bastard-- -Knock it off!

720
47:18.815 --> 47:20.025
-Stop. -Let go.

721
47:20.108 --> 47:21.777
I'll kill that bastard today!

722
47:21.860 --> 47:25.364
That's Mr. Sato Hideo. He's going to marry our boss's daughter!

723
47:33.538 --> 47:34.665
Sato?

724
47:51.848 --> 47:55.310
I'm still shaken up over that incident at the banquet.

725
47:56.812 --> 47:58.605
You weren't hurt, were you?

726
47:59.731 --> 48:00.565
No, I'm fine.

727
48:09.658 --> 48:12.160
What did you think of the newspaper article?

728
48:12.244 --> 48:13.620
I arranged it in a hurry.

729
48:14.329 --> 48:16.331
It was very timely.

730
48:16.415 --> 48:18.166
I'm glad.

731
48:18.250 --> 48:20.377
I wanted to do something for the Government-General…

732
48:20.460 --> 48:23.630
Or rather, for you, as family.

733
48:26.591 --> 48:29.886
I arranged the sale of government property in Gyodang-ri

734
48:29.970 --> 48:32.806
so I could repay you someday down the line--

735
48:32.889 --> 48:34.307
Please keep your voice down.

736
48:36.685 --> 48:37.978
If there's nothing else,

737
48:38.562 --> 48:39.771
I'll get going.

738
48:43.608 --> 48:47.612
I was 16 when I first went into business.

739
48:49.656 --> 48:51.533
My late father used to say,

740
48:52.743 --> 48:54.327
"Once a scale tips to one side,

741
48:55.245 --> 48:58.331
it's bound to tip again. Don't bother fixing it."

742
49:08.675 --> 49:11.511
I straightened things out for you this once.

743
49:12.512 --> 49:14.347
But if you go off balance again,

744
49:15.182 --> 49:19.603
then I'll have to invest in a new scale.

745
49:34.910 --> 49:35.994
We're terribly sorry.

746
49:36.495 --> 49:39.247
You're Mr. Sato Hideo, the son of Inspector General Sato

747
49:39.331 --> 49:41.291
at the Government-General, right?

748
49:44.711 --> 49:45.879
The Government-General?

749
49:46.379 --> 49:48.507
We work for Joil Textile Factory.

750
49:48.590 --> 49:51.301
Please forgive our rudeness.

751
49:52.010 --> 49:52.928
Hey.

752
49:53.011 --> 49:54.679
My apologies, Mr. Sato Hideo.

753
49:54.763 --> 49:55.806
Please forgive me!

754
49:57.015 --> 49:58.725
I'm not the one who deserves your apology.

755
49:59.768 --> 50:00.644
Pardon?

756
50:01.228 --> 50:02.562
Yes, sir.

757
50:02.646 --> 50:04.731
We're terribly sorry. Please forgive us.

758
50:04.815 --> 50:06.233
What a cutie.

759
50:07.275 --> 50:09.277
We were only here on our boss's orders

760
50:09.361 --> 50:11.363
to notify the residents about the relocation.

761
50:11.446 --> 50:12.697
We meant nothing else by it.

762
50:13.365 --> 50:14.825
-You should leave now. -Sorry?

763
50:15.826 --> 50:17.828
Yes, sir. Come on, hurry.

764
50:19.746 --> 50:21.331
They're leaving just like that?

765
50:27.629 --> 50:29.506
Good grief, the teacher was…

766
50:29.589 --> 50:30.841
Kkot-nim's teacher…

767
50:32.008 --> 50:32.843
I'm sorry.

768
50:36.555 --> 50:37.389
I'm sorry.

769
50:46.148 --> 50:46.982
Is it true?

770
50:53.989 --> 50:55.866
Tell me. Is it really true?

771
50:57.617 --> 50:59.035
Why aren't you answering me?

772
51:03.582 --> 51:05.584
Are you really

773
51:05.667 --> 51:08.128
the son of someone important at the Government-General?

774
51:09.588 --> 51:12.007
And you're marrying into the Joil Textile family?

775
51:14.801 --> 51:15.927
What's your deal?

776
51:16.761 --> 51:19.556
Was teaching Kkot-nim to read all part of some scheme?

777
51:19.639 --> 51:20.473
What for?

778
51:21.141 --> 51:24.019
What are you planning to do here after driving us all out?

779
51:24.686 --> 51:26.938
Do we look like a joke to you?

780
51:31.026 --> 51:32.194
That's enough, No-ma.

781
51:33.904 --> 51:34.738
What?

782
51:37.866 --> 51:40.285
Things aren't always what they seem.

783
51:40.368 --> 51:43.121
So don't judge when you don't know the whole story.

784
51:43.205 --> 51:44.581
Are you

785
51:45.165 --> 51:46.333
taking his side now?

786
51:47.417 --> 51:48.627
No, that's not it.

787
51:49.169 --> 51:50.003
Ga-kyung!

788
51:51.504 --> 51:53.548
Since you work with Japs at the Government-General,

789
51:53.632 --> 51:54.966
do you think you're Japanese now?

790
51:55.592 --> 51:57.552
Do you even know who he is?

791
51:57.636 --> 52:00.472
His father is the leader of the Jap bastards who stole our country

792
52:00.555 --> 52:03.475
and his father-in-law is a traitor who's trying to drive us out.

793
52:04.476 --> 52:06.311
No-ma. Just hear me out.

794
52:08.396 --> 52:10.023
Oh, I see. You…

795
52:10.607 --> 52:12.234
Don't tell me you like this guy.

796
52:26.414 --> 52:27.249
So it's true.

797
52:28.750 --> 52:32.295
First you serve the Japs like a dog, and now you're messing around with one?

798
52:32.379 --> 52:33.338
Just like your mom?

799
52:54.359 --> 52:55.193
Ga-kyung.

800
52:55.986 --> 52:57.237
That's not what I meant.

801
52:57.320 --> 52:58.321
You're right.

802
52:59.948 --> 53:02.325
I'm the daughter of a woman who slept with a Japanese man.

803
53:05.870 --> 53:06.705
Ga-kyung.

804
53:42.490 --> 53:43.325
I'm sorry.

805
53:43.408 --> 53:44.659
You seem to have a fever.

806
53:45.285 --> 53:47.537
You may have overdone it going out today.

807
53:48.913 --> 53:49.831
Get some rest.

808
53:51.082 --> 53:52.000
I want Seo-hee…

809
53:53.960 --> 53:56.755
to go to America, not Shanghai.

810
53:57.714 --> 53:59.507
I want to keep my word to her.

811
53:59.591 --> 54:00.759
Yes, I understand.

812
54:02.052 --> 54:04.804
But I can't guarantee it.

813
54:04.888 --> 54:05.889
I'll do what I can.

814
54:05.972 --> 54:07.265
I know you can.

815
54:11.061 --> 54:12.437
Please marry her.

816
54:15.148 --> 54:18.276
Just as you married me and got me an American passport,

817
54:19.277 --> 54:20.820
I want you to marry her

818
54:20.904 --> 54:23.782
and get her an American passport so she can go to America.

819
54:25.742 --> 54:26.576
So-ran.

820
54:26.659 --> 54:28.703
Once I kill Sato,

821
54:30.455 --> 54:33.458
I won't need an American passport anymore.

822
54:33.541 --> 54:34.376
So-ran.

823
54:53.937 --> 54:54.938
Listen, So-ran.

824
54:58.149 --> 55:01.027
I do think there's a chance she turned on us.

825
55:01.111 --> 55:04.072
That's what being a spy does. It eats you up inside.

826
55:04.155 --> 55:06.282
Still, I suggested we send her to Shanghai

827
55:06.366 --> 55:09.035
because you worry about her and care about her.

828
55:09.119 --> 55:10.495
It is all for you.

829
55:12.872 --> 55:14.332
Now you want me to marry her?

830
55:22.048 --> 55:25.385
I married you because you're you, So-ran. Because it was you.

831
55:27.429 --> 55:29.347
And now you're telling me…

832
55:31.850 --> 55:34.436
you're going to die right before my very eyes.

833
55:46.990 --> 55:51.244
Watching you run a high fever all night, I was terrified…

834
55:56.749 --> 55:57.625
I'd lose you.

835
57:17.247 --> 57:18.790
So she's not

836
57:19.290 --> 57:20.416
Keum Seok-jung's wife?

837
57:20.500 --> 57:21.334
No, sir.

838
57:21.834 --> 57:24.045
We questioned everyone in Kyeam-ri.

839
57:24.837 --> 57:26.256
-Is this woman -Is this woman

840
57:26.339 --> 57:28.675
-Keum Seok-jung's wife? -Keum Seok-jung's wife?

841
57:31.052 --> 57:32.178
They say it's not her.

842
57:37.267 --> 57:39.978
Every single one said she wasn't Keum Seok-jung's wife.

843
57:41.187 --> 57:42.272
But

844
57:42.355 --> 57:45.108
I think we finally got a lead on them.

845
57:47.193 --> 57:49.821
The name of Keum Seok-jung's dead daughter was…

846
57:49.904 --> 57:51.364
No, it's not her.

847
57:51.447 --> 57:53.157
Seo-hee's mom was ugly.

848
57:53.241 --> 57:54.742
She wasn't this pretty.

849
57:55.243 --> 57:58.037
She said Seo-hee's mom didn't look this beautiful.

850
57:59.205 --> 58:00.248
…Seo-hee.

851
58:00.873 --> 58:03.126
Keum Seo-hee. That was her name.

852
58:04.002 --> 58:05.295
Keum Seo-hee.

853
58:08.214 --> 58:09.090
Yes.

854
58:11.217 --> 58:13.219
Dinner at your residence tomorrow?

855
58:14.178 --> 58:15.054
That's right.

856
58:15.722 --> 58:17.473
I'd like you to bring your wife.

857
58:51.382 --> 58:52.216
We're here.

858
58:53.134 --> 58:55.762
Yes, we are.

859
59:05.563 --> 59:06.564
Well…

860
59:07.940 --> 59:09.567
About what No-ma said,

861
59:10.151 --> 59:10.985
I hope…

862
59:13.071 --> 59:15.657
you don't take it too hard.

863
59:17.992 --> 59:18.826
All right.

864
59:25.792 --> 59:27.251
Don't worry about Gyodang-ri.

865
59:27.752 --> 59:29.629
I'll try to persuade Mr. Kim.

866
59:31.089 --> 59:34.801
Why would you… do that?

867
59:43.935 --> 59:45.436
Can you trust me?

868
59:49.482 --> 59:52.485
No matter what I do or say?

869
59:54.904 --> 59:57.281
You don't have to answer me right now.

870
59:58.199 --> 59:59.033
But…

871
01:00:02.078 --> 01:00:03.037
for now…

872
01:00:04.706 --> 01:00:06.124
I just want you to trust me.

873
01:00:14.674 --> 01:00:15.508
Lee Ga-kyung.

874
01:00:15.591 --> 01:00:16.426
Yes?

875
01:00:20.179 --> 01:00:21.305
I mean…

876
01:00:21.389 --> 01:00:22.724
I wasn't answering you.

877
01:00:22.807 --> 01:00:24.308
Lee Ga-kyung suits you…

878
01:00:27.437 --> 01:00:29.147
much better than Keum Seo-hee.

879
01:00:37.447 --> 01:00:39.365
Lee Ga-kyung.

880
01:00:44.370 --> 01:00:46.122
May I call you that?

881
01:00:52.545 --> 01:00:54.338
I do want an answer to that now.

882
01:00:58.551 --> 01:00:59.469
Mom.

883
01:01:07.852 --> 01:01:09.562
When I'm with him,

884
01:01:11.314 --> 01:01:12.940
I don't want to be Keum Seo-hee.

885
01:01:13.649 --> 01:01:16.319
I want to be Lee Ga-kyung.

886
01:01:18.780 --> 01:01:20.198
Without deception.

887
01:01:21.199 --> 01:01:22.033
Just…

888
01:01:22.784 --> 01:01:23.785
as myself.

889
01:01:28.956 --> 01:01:32.168
But I'm a spy.

890
01:01:33.252 --> 01:01:34.921
I shouldn't be doing this.

891
01:01:37.548 --> 01:01:38.424
Yes…

892
01:01:42.011 --> 01:01:44.722
Interpreter Kim Tae-ung.

893
01:02:00.071 --> 01:02:02.365
It's too late to go back.

894
01:02:03.866 --> 01:02:05.159
What do I do?

895
01:02:06.035 --> 01:02:06.953
Mom.

896
01:02:48.953 --> 01:02:51.581
100 DAYS OF DECEPTION

897
01:02:51.664 --> 01:02:53.291
This has to be a trap.

898
01:02:53.374 --> 01:02:56.586
Do you want us to arrest Keum Seo-hee tonight?

899
01:02:56.669 --> 01:02:58.337
We have no more time to waste.

900
01:02:58.421 --> 01:02:59.922
We need to do whatever we can.

901
01:03:00.006 --> 01:03:01.215
This pneumatic tube thing

902
01:03:01.299 --> 01:03:03.843
is more than big enough to fit a bomb.

903
01:03:03.926 --> 01:03:06.512
We could get a bomb into their hands in two and a half minutes?

904
01:03:07.179 --> 01:03:08.764
Didn't I just tell you?

905
01:03:08.848 --> 01:03:10.224
No one leaves the building.

906
01:03:10.308 --> 01:03:11.851
I said I had something prepared.

907
01:03:14.896 --> 01:03:15.730
I think Keum Seo-hee

908
01:03:17.481 --> 01:03:18.983
is a spy.

909
01:03:29.035 --> 01:03:31.037
Subtitle translation by: Youji Kim
